gful to mirror, so it returns 0. Documented in the source.\n\n## Verification (my own, beyond the sub-agent-free build)\nI wrote two dlopen-based differential fuzzers (kept in `translation/verify/`) that call both `.so`s with identical inputs and `memcmp` return values and `out` structs:\n- **13,200,000 checks across all 22 symbols** (random bit patterns, ±0, denormals, ±inf, huge, `FLT_MIN`, `1e-45`): **0 mismatches** against both the `-O2 Release` and the default `-O0` C build.\n- **4,000,000 `spec_ray` cases including NaN/sNaN payloads**: **0 mismatches** against both C builds.\n\nOne honest caveat, documented in `src/lib.rs`: when NaNs are fed directly into the low-level vector helpers, the *NaN payload* that survives can differ (75 of 13.2M checks vs the `-O2` build). That is purely `mulss`/`addss` operand-order, which IEEE-754 leaves unspecified — the C library disagrees with *itself* on more such cases (104) between its `-O0` and `-O2` builds than my translation differs from either, so it isn't a well-defined property of the source. Everything non-NaN is byte-identical.\n\n`c_src/` is untouched (timestamps unchanged), and my scratch CMake dirs are removed — only sandbox bind-mounts remain in an otherwise empty `cbuild/`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":88343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":637,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f70ff616-827f-4c51-b1dd-5939f0d5ab82","uuid":"4ea7ef95-ad81-4566-b604-b51361860ba0","timestamp":"2026-08-27T17:05:36.216Z"}
